<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eberhard I, Count of Württemberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1265–1325</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Eberhard the Illustrious</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eberhard I, called the Illustrious, was Count of Württemberg from 1279 to 1325. He fought the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and the Swabian imperial cities, and lost most of his lands in 1312 to forces acting for Emperor Henry VII, but recovered them after the emperor's death. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a> the residence of the counts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eberhard-i-count-of-wurttemberg.jpg" alt="Eberhard I, Count of Württemberg" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christian Friedrich Sattler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eberhard_I_vW_Sattler.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
